  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1244 AM MDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nMonsoon moisture remains in place through Thursday, with the\ndeepest moisture across eastern Idaho for today. Today will a\nbit of a higher risk of decent downpours vs tomorrow. Where\nstorms fire today, the risk of gusts over 35 mph is likely with\nstrongest gusts potentially peaking around 55-60 mph.\nThunderstorm coverage is going to be dependent on where we see\nmore sun breaks today, as smoke is still around in some places\nand/or we can overcome morning cloud cover. Going into tomorrow,\nwe are going to maintain isolated overnight storms (similar to\nthis morning), and 15-25% coverage tomorrow. There is a 25-50%\nchance for gusts over 35 mph, potentially peaking at 45-50 mph.\nTemperatures will be cooler today with highs in the mid 80s to\nlower 90s, pushing tomorrow through the 80s into the mid 90s in\nsome locations. \n\nFriday and Saturday still look hot, very dry, and breezy.\nTemperatures will be in the low 90s for even \"cooler valleys\"\nthis time of year with warmer spots pushing low to mid 100s.\nThis will rapidly increase HeatRisk impacts across most of\ncentral and eastern Idaho. The stretch is short, but still\nimportant enough to take precautions to prevent heat-related\nissues and also check on those more vulnerable in these\nconditions. We do see temperatures dropping heading into next\nweek, BUT it will remain really dry and breezy at times. This is\nthe result of the ridge breaking down, but at the moment the\nflow remains more westerly vs. returning to southwesterly. This\nwill keep drier air in place. Temperatures actually return to\nAVERAGE for beginning of August.",
